  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Tied through three, they held the lead in the fourth, then let it slip in the fifth and never got it back.",
    "what_this_means": "The moment arrived in inning one with runners in scoring position. Nothing came of it. That was the pattern. Seven hits across nine innings, but four runners left in scoring position with nothing to show. Machado and France each drove in a run, enough to stay in the game, but not enough to close it. Sears gave them six quality innings, and the bullpen held. Peralta, Rodriguez, Hart all threw clean. But it didn't matter. Atlanta scored twice in the fifth and that was the difference. This is what inconsistency looks like from the inside: the bats touch the game without changing it. They had the opening. They closed nothing.",
    "what_to_watch": "Reynaldo L\u00f3pez takes the mound tonight against Walker Buehler, a 3.50 ERA matchup that favors control over power. Exactly the kind of pitcher who will expose an offense that left four runners on base in a one-run loss.",
